{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1465240-v20-clarification-about-vehicle-maneuverability","id":1465240,"title":"[V20] Clarification about vehicle maneuverability","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-24T21:47:11-07:00","id":1465240,"title":"[V20] Clarification about vehicle maneuverability","content":"The V20 source book says that the most dice a driver can have in their driving pool is equal to the maneuver rating of the vehicle they are in. As the majority of passenger vehicles have a maneuver rating of 6, what purpose does it serve to have a getaway driver ever have more than one or two dots in Drive? Or for a stunt driver to have the Daredevil merit since the bonus dice will literally never come into play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27140-doctor-awkward","name":"Doctor Awkward","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T01:39:30-07:00","id":1465256,"title":"","content":"A customized vehicle will have a higher maneuverability. If you want to get more out of your car, tune it accordingly.<br /> <br /> Most getaway drivers won't rely on speed or maneuverability either, focusing on not getting attention to begin with, so depending on the driver, putting many dots on Drive isn't a thing to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T12:31:33-07:00","id":1465307,"title":"","content":"If you want to use those awesome Rockford Files J-Turns, just get a higher performance car that is still seen as normal, but is more sporty. <br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5X7XGmS6Pe4\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=5X7XGmS6Pe4\" data-code=\"5X7XGmS6Pe4\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/5X7XGmS6Pe4/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Those should have higher maneuverability rating. And if they don't, talk to the ST. After all, Jim Rockford used a Pontiac Firebird Esprit, not a Grand Am. Steve McQueen in Bullitt drove a Ford Mustang, not a Ford Pinto. The Duke Brothers in the Dukes of Hazzard had a Dodge Charger as the General Lee, not a Dodge Dart. Yet none of those cars would look out of the ordinary on the roads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T14:05:29-07:00","id":1465320,"title":"","content":"Precisely. The maneuverability rules are there because there is a hard limit on what the car can do, no matter how good you are. And driving a better car won't make you a better driver, either. But will give you more options if you ARE a better driver.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-25T21:49:25-07:00","id":1465356,"title":"","content":"I would ignore the rules except in cases where the manouverability of the vehicle is super important. <br /> <br /> Racing down a highway with large spaces between vehicles? Doesn't matter<br /> Racing through a dense pedestrian area and trying to avoid civilians? Hugely important. <br /> <br /> <br /> I would also use the caps creatively. <br /> IE, if you have eight dice for driving and shooting, but your vehicle has a six die limit, the player can use six dice for driving and two for shooting or whatever<br /> <br /> IMO, If you're getting into heated car chases with police, you've already lost (even if you can get away) and vampires are city bound and don't get out much, So these things rarely happen in my game","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-26T04:53:15-07:00","id":1465380,"title":"","content":"Splitting dice is another huge advantage of having a higher pool than your Maneuverability, that's for sure. I wouldn't ignore it in easier situations because I'm not even sure a roll is necessary on then and the car is the car. But being able to split your pool for complex navigation (let's lose them!), shooting and other stuff, that's a must.<br /> <br /> Although even that is for a more cinematic game. For anything more grounded <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> is right, if you're being chased you already lost. Nowadays you can even confirm with books and YouTube videos from real ex-criminals about the matter, the whole point of a getaway is not being chased to begin with. And a stunt driver wouldn't use a common car right out of the factory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}